<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kirti Sri Rajasinha</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">reigned <a href="/years/1747">1747</a>–<a href="/years/1782">1782</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kirti Sri Rajasinha was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a> from 1747 to 1782, of the Nayak dynasty of south Indian origin. A patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>, he invited monks from Siam in 1753 to restore the higher ordination, founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siyam-nikaya">Siyam Nikaya</a>, and restored many temples. He fought a war with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, who took Kandy in 1765 and imposed a treaty in 1766.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kirti-sri-rajasinha.jpg" alt="Kirti Sri Rajasinha" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photo Dharma from Sadao, Thailand · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:118_King_Rajasingha_makes_Ven_Saranankara_Sangharaja_(19820173144).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
